We need to create the same package name in the consumer as the producer package name to ensure that the event classes can be properly serialized and deserialized. For example:

- **Producer Package Name:** `com.prudhviraj.ecommerce.kafka.user_svc.events`
- **Consumer Package Name:** `com.prudhviraj.ecommerce.kafka.user_svc.events`

This consistency in package structure allows the consumer to locate and process the events produced by the producer without encountering trust issues or serialization errors.